 # Changelog
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- **Review gate escapes need an operator act.** A `Not verified: N` line in report.md no longer passes unverified blocker or major findings, and a report first line saying the PR moved no longer passes readiness item `head`. Both need the operator's `--waive verifier` or `--waive head`. `review complete --head` with a head other than the recorded one needs `--head-reason "<operator quote>"`. A waiver now lifts only its own item's research errors. `review publish` runs the same close gates as `review complete`. [#1166](https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1166)
+- **Breaking for packages closed through the removed escapes.** A package that an earlier release closed on a `Not verified: N` line or a first-line head statement now reads NOT READY in `review readiness`, `status` and the panel, and `review publish` refuses it. Repair: the operator waives the item (`keryx review complete <package> --waive verifier|head "<their words>"`), or publish it with `--partial`. [#1166](https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1166)
+
+## [0.4.27] - 2026-11-13
+
+### Added
+
+- **Searchable Shell history.** Open the current session archive with `/history` or `Ctrl+Shift+H` in Agent and Chat Shell. Search as you type, use Find or Enter to jump, and move between matches with Up and Down. Readline mode prints the conversation with `/history`. [#1167](https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1167)
+- **Diagnostics for stalled tool calls.** The Shell records snapshots of stalled calls and their current stages. Use `/diag` to capture a snapshot on demand. [#1165](https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1165)
+
+### Changed
+
+- **Session resume and switching.** The Shell restores up to 20 visible messages from the last turn, including assistant replies, and preserves agent attribution in the archive. History loads in chunks as you scroll, and search runs asynchronously across the archive, including long messages. [#1167](https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1167)
+
+### Fixed
+
+- **Hub cancellation receipts.** If Session Host cannot prove that a turn stopped, the receipt reports `recovery-required`. [#1167](https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1167)
+
 ## [0.4.26] - 2026-11-12
 
 ### Fixed
 
 - **Shell approval and draft recovery.** A command runs only after an explicit allow choice. Esc dismisses approval, and Enter defaults to denial. Esc in the busy recipient picker restores the draft without submitting it to Main or Side-1. [#1160](https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1160)
 - **Session resume and switching.** Resumed sessions keep their full conversation and archive. Switching clears the previous transcript and usage, preserves pending input for explicit submission, and keeps delayed replies in their original session. [#1160](https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1160)
 - **Escape interrupts active Agent and Chat turns.** The shell remains available for a follow-up. An open modal handles Escape before it reaches the active turn. [#1160](https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1160)
 
 ### Verification
 
 - CI runs the Hub recovery and unattended sandbox suites on Ubuntu 26.04 and fails if they are skipped. The Hub tests track the supervised shell across restarts, and the socket scan has its own deadline. [#1162](https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1162)
 - The flow 487 journal records closure and links to the final terminal captures. [#1161](https://github.com/MrCipherSmith/keryx/pull/1161)
 
 ## [0.4.25] - 2026-11-10
 
 ### Fixed
 - **Session token and cost totals in the shell footer and `/status` no longer inflate with every turn.** Usage events used to be counted once per earlier turn, so turn N was counted N times. A single usage sink is now installed once per shell and each turn attaches to it and detaches when the turn ends. The per-turn cost also no longer gets overwritten by an older turn.
 
 ### Changed
 - **The usage footer is coloured and drops the key hint.** Input tokens, output tokens and cost use distinct theme roles. While usage is shown, the `/ commands · Ctrl+C cancels a turn` hint is omitted; it still appears before the first turn.

